Committee: Ways and Means Education
Sponsor: Orr
Analyst: Daniel Davenport
Date: 04/22/2021
FISCAL NOTE
Senate Bill 189 as substituted and reported by the Committee on Ways and Means Education appropriates $7,655,660,674 from the Education Trust Fund (ETF) to various state agencies, entities, institutions, and public schools for the support, maintenance, and development of public education in Alabama for the fiscal year ending September 30, 2022.
In addition, for the fiscal year ending September 30, 2022, this act appropriates the following amounts to the following entities from the following other state funds:
*$210,532,864, est. from the Public School Fund to the State Board of Education for public schools;
*$2,000,000 from the Alabama Peace Officers' Standards and Training Fund to the Alabama Peace Officers' Standards and Training Commission;
*$5,144,570 from the Driver Education and Training Fund to the Department of Education;
*$5,000,000 from the Special Education Catastrophic Fund to the Department of Education;
*$50,000,000 from the TEAMS Fund to the State Board of Education - Local Boards of Education;
*$6,500,000 from the Supercomputer Revolving Fund to the Alabama Supercomputer Authority;
*$122,207, est. from the Music Hall of Fame Fund to Music Hall of Fame;
*$8,635,769 from the Alabama Board of Nursing Trust Fund to the Alabama Board of Nursing;
*$2,000,000 from the ACS Truck Driver Fund to the Alabama Community College System;
*$1,000,000 from the Alabama Head and Spinal Cord Injury Trust Fund to the Department of Rehabilitation Services;
*$10,000,000 from the Dual Enrollment Tax Credit Fund to the Alabama Community College System; and
*$6,000,000 from the Children's Policy Council Fund to the Department of Early Childhood Education.
In addition, this bill appropriates $10,783,869,237 from federal and other funds for the fiscal year ending September 30, 2022.
Bill Poole, Chair
Ways and Means Education

